-| REQ-PUBLISH-042 | Local Diagram-Generation Backend (paperbanana + ERNIE-Image-Turbo) | Implemented, live-verified | Operator directive 2026-07-21: gemini/claude/codex API tokens no longer available, so diagram generation must run local-only. Vendored `external/paperbanana` (MIT, gitignored) at latest tag v0.3.0, unmodified; `python/carnot/imagegen/ernie_image_server.py` is a local FastAPI shim implementing paperbanana's `OpenAIImageGen` request/response contract (`POST /v1/images/generations`), backed by `baidu/ERNIE-Image-Turbo` (Apache-2.0, Diffusers-native, 8B-param distilled DiT, loaded via `diffusers.ErnieImagePipeline`) as a lazy singleton with an honest `RuntimeError` when the model is not yet cached (never silently downloads); `scripts/generate_diagram.py` is the new entrypoint, `CARNOT_IMAGE_BACKEND` defaults to `ernie-local`. SAME-DAY REVISION 2026-07-21: switched from the base `baidu/ERNIE-Image` (50 steps, guidance_scale=4.0) to the Turbo variant (8 steps, guidance_scale=1.0) per a follow-up operator directive — confirmed via the Turbo model's own HuggingFace card that guidance_scale=1.0 is correct for the distilled checkpoint (reusing the base model's 4.0 would likely degrade output, not just change speed); neither variant's weights had been downloaded before this revision, so no prior real generation needed reconciling. Known gap documented (not hidden): the VLM planner/critic/stylist role still defaults to a paid provider; a visible warning is printed rather than silently proceeding. SECOND SAME-DAY REVISION 2026-07-21: `use_pe` (the pipeline's own prompt-rewriting auxiliary LLM, confirmed via `inspect.signature(ErnieImagePipeline.__call__)` to default `True`) is now explicitly passed `False` — read `_enhance_prompt_with_pe` in the installed `diffusers` source directly to confirm it runs a separate LLM `.generate()` call to rewrite the prompt, which would silently override paperbanana's own engineered prompt if left at its default. THIRD SAME-DAY REVISION 2026-07-21: weights downloaded (31.63GB, 24 files, verified complete via `scan_cache_dir` against the repo's own reported file count) and LIVE-VERIFIED end-to-end for the first time — the first real (non-mocked) load hit a genuine `torch.OutOfMemoryError` (a bare `.to(device)` moves the unused 7.66GB `pe` submodel to GPU anyway, pushing total demand to ~31GB against a 24GB card); fixed by dropping `pipe.pe`/`pipe.pe_tokenizer` (both `Optional[...] = None` in the pipeline's own constructor) and using `enable_model_cpu_offload` instead of `.to(device)`. Re-verified: 14.1s load, 16.67GB peak VRAM, real 1024x1024 image generated in 56.6s at 8 steps (visually confirmed correct: legible "A", "B", "C" text, correctly connected boxes matching the test prompt), clean 0 MiB GPU release afterward. |
-| SCENARIO-PUBLISH-042 | ernie-local Backend Serves paperbanana Without Paid API Keys | Implemented, live-verified | 13 tests in `tests/python/test_ernie_image_server.py`, all mocked (no GPU/network/8B download): request/response contract (size-string parsing, b64_json round-trip via PIL, n=1 enforcement returning HTTP 400 for n=2), healthz cache-state reporting, the honest-RuntimeError-on-uncached-model precondition path, an explicit assertion that `guidance_scale=1.0`/`num_inference_steps=8` are passed to the pipeline (not the base model's `4.0`/`50`), and an explicit assertion that `use_pe=False` reaches the pipeline call, verified to bind against the REAL `ErnieImagePipeline.__call__` signature via `inspect.signature(...).bind_partial(...)` (not just the mocked stub). Manually verified `scripts/generate_diagram.py --backend none` and `--backend ernie-local` end-to-end. PLUS a real, non-mocked smoke test exercising the actual production `ErniePipelineSingleton.get()` + pipeline call (not a reimplementation) after the weights were downloaded: found and fixed a real CUDA OOM (see REQ-PUBLISH-042 row), then re-ran and confirmed a real 1024x1024 image generates correctly. |
